msgid "UBlox GPS Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:7
#: 021dc9edb1e84fa08bbc7fc6c1136703
msgid "This article explains how to connect to u-center to change the configuration of a :ref:`3DR uBlox <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-compass-module>` module. This is not expected to be necessary for normal users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:14
#: 5b55bbe6a9f245a6b8a9d22ea03aeb72
msgid "Connection Option #1 - Mission Planner and Pixhawk as Passthrough"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:16
#: d1f16a1154a14888b6223ccbd358e6e9
msgid "Mission planner and pixhawk can pass through the communication between u-center and the GPS by doing the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:19
#: 0b7fc615bf8f4cd3a38506dd9152117a
msgid "Connect Pixhawk to your PC and connect with the Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:20
#: a3be47d880c8499a84d3f086055bf8a3
msgid "On the Flight Data screen press Ctrl-F and then select \"MAVSerial pass\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:21
#: df1ed5ad5a9f404ba80e5474b8acfada
msgid "Open u-center and select Receiver, TCP Client and in the Network Connection window set Address to \"localhost\" and Port to \"500\" and press OK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:23
#: 9de855d683f0431aaf923673e9705e12
msgid "See instructions below as to how to upload config with u-center."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:32
#: bbd92131a90d46959527083d41fe16ae
msgid "Connection Option #2 - FTDI cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ublox-gps.rst:34
#: 8cb7a5525fcf4011b1757e3d563397b4
msgid "You will need an `FTDI cable <https://www.amazon.com/ftdi-adapter/s?k=ftdi+adapter>`__ and a `GPS adapter cable <http://store.scoutuav.com/product/cables-connectors/gps-cable-10-cm/>`__ to connect the GPS to your computer. If you have never plugged an FTDI device into your computer, you may need to download and install the `Virtual COM port driver <http://www.ftdichip.com/Drivers/VCP.htm>`__."
msgstr ""
